## 1.7.0-5v
5 V-input hardware variant (modules/16bit-5v), derived from 16bit 1.6.0 (hardware) /
1.7.0 (firmware history below is unchanged - the same apps and binaries run on both).

- The module's supply socket (V_SUPPLY1, all five pins) now takes the **5 V** slot rail
  instead of 3.3 V. Nothing on the module runs from 5 V after the new regulator.
- New **U6 AP2112K-3.3** (Diodes, SOT-23-5, LCSC C51118, MPN AP2112K-3.3TRG1), 600 mA
  low-dropout LDO: VIN and EN from the new +5V net, VOUT onto the existing +3V3 rail,
  which keeps every load the original 3.3 V net drove.
- New input decoupling next to the regulator: **C25 10 uF/25 V 0805** (C15850) and
  **C26 100 nF 0402** (C1525); new output capacitor **C27 1 uF/50 V 0805** (C28323).
  The 3.3 V rail keeps its existing local bulk (C19 10 uF, C21 100 uF).
  A PWR_FLAG documents that +5V is externally supplied by the base slot.
- PCB: the 5 V input path is routed on B.Cu - 0.8 mm bus across the five supply pins and
  the trunk to the regulator, 0.6 mm taps to VIN/EN and the input capacitors; the old
  3.3 V feed from the supply pins is removed and the +3V3 distribution is now fed by the
  LDO (one short B.Cu bridge re-joins the two pre-existing +3V3 pour pockets).
- `modules/16bit/code` (firmware) is intentionally **not** copied: the firmware is
  unchanged by this variant and `code/16bit/lib/lfs` is a git submodule.
- `production/` holds this variant's own BOM/CPL/IPC netlist/gerbers (`16bit-5v.*`);
  the original module's historical `production/backups/` archives are not carried over.
- The board file is saved by the KiCad 10 toolchain (same generator version as
  modules/32bit); the schematic keeps its original KiCad 8 format with minimal edits.

## 1.7.0
Add the MIDI-clock-synced motion recorder (MODE button) to the polysynth app.
It records 4 bars of CV1/CV2 + MCC Bank A (CC20..23) per take and loops it.
Move the shared recorder header to `includes/audio/apps/motion_recorder.h`
(previously under `monosynth/`) so both synth apps use the same state machine.

## 1.6.0
Change the filter of the Delay FX into an Highpass filter

## 1.5.3
